--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Splunk Common Information Model (CIM) add-on
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/engine/cim/cimModelsData.ts contains CIM dataset names, field names, and
tag constraints derived from the Splunk Common Information Model add-on
(Splunk_SA_CIM), distributed by Splunk Inc. on Splunkbase under Splunk's own
licence terms:

    https://splunkbase.splunk.com/app/1621

The add-on is not vendored, redistributed, or fetched by this repository. It is
not required to build, test, or run Propslab. Generation from it
(scripts/generate-cim-models.js) is a manual, occasional step run by a
maintainer against their own separately obtained copy, and nothing in the build
or install path invokes it.

The generated file is committed so that the build is reproducible without the
add-on. The material it carries — dataset and field identifiers, and which tags
a dataset constraint requires — is factual naming needed to check whether an
extraction is CIM-compliant. It is used here for interoperability, and it is
not offered under this project's MIT licence. Rights in the CIM add-on and its
data models remain with Splunk Inc.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Configuration directive documentation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/engine/directiveRegistry.ts describes the props.conf and transforms.conf
attributes this simulator recognises. Those descriptions are written for this
project. Where they restate what an attribute does, they describe documented,
observable behaviour of the software; they are not copied from Splunk's
documentation or from the .spec files that ship with Splunk Enterprise, and
those files are not reproduced here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fidelity fixtures
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/engine/__tests__/fixtures/splunk-<version>/ holds recorded outputs of a
Splunk Enterprise instance processing small synthetic inputs, used to assert
that this simulator's behaviour matches the real one. They record functional
results only. No performance measurement, benchmark, or comparative evaluation
of Splunk software is conducted or published by this project. The set committed
here was recorded in August 2026 from Splunk Enterprise 10.4.0 by the
maintainer, whose property those results are under section 18.2 of the Splunk
General Terms. No capture tooling ships with this repository and no further
capture is planned; src/engine/__tests__/fixtures/README.md explains why.
